export default [
{slug:'cash-flow-opening-closing-balance',title:'Follow cash from opening balance to the next period',category:'money',summary:'Model receipts and payments in order without confusing cash flow with profit or a balanced monthly budget.',tools:['cash-flow','budget-planner','invoice-builder'],sources:['cashTiming','businessCash'],sections:[
{title:'Track when money actually moves',paragraphs:['A cash-flow table describes receipts and payments over a sequence of periods. The opening balance starts the first period. Each closing balance becomes the next opening balance. This makes timing visible in a way that a single annual total cannot.','Use one currency and a consistent basis for each row. A weekly table should use receipts and payments expected within that week. An invoice issued today is not necessarily cash received today. The tool does not connect to bank accounts or determine tax treatment; it models the figures you enter.']},
{title:'Check the carry-forward arithmetic',paragraphs:['The rule is opening cash plus receipts minus payments equals closing cash. If opening cash is NPR 10,000, receipts are 15,000 and payments are 18,000, the closing balance is 7000. The next row starts at 7000 automatically.','If the next period receives 5000 and pays 9000, it closes at 3000. The combined two-period change is receipts of 20,000 minus payments of 27,000, a reduction of 7000 from the original 10,000. These two ways of checking the total should agree.'],table:{headers:['Period','Opening','Receipts','Payments','Closing'],rows:[['1','10,000','15,000','18,000','7000'],['2','7000','5000','9000','3000']]}},
{title:'Choose periods that reveal the risk',paragraphs:['A monthly row can hide a shortfall between an early bill and a late receipt. If timing matters, use shorter periods and place entries when they are expected to clear. A negative modeled closing balance identifies a gap under those assumptions. It does not tell you which funding or spending decision is appropriate.'],list:['Set the starting cash and currency.','Enter periods in chronological order.','Add expected receipts and payments for each period.','Review the first negative or unusually low balance.','Export the table and compare it with actual records later.']},
{title:'Keep estimates separate from accounting records',paragraphs:['Cash flow is not the same as profit. Borrowing, capital purchases, unpaid invoices and other items can affect cash and accounting results differently. This simple planner does not create accounts, reconcile statements or produce an audited financial report.','Use clear row labels, document uncertain receipts and test an alternate timing scenario when helpful. Save on this device is optional and uses browser storage, which can be cleared. Export a backup and retain the underlying records. When actual money arrives or leaves, update the figures and investigate differences rather than assuming the original forecast remains accurate.']}
]},
{slug:'manual-inventory-stock-value-reorder',title:'Keep a manual inventory with stock value and reorder flags',category:'business',summary:'Use unique SKUs, a defined unit cost and a real count before relying on stock totals.',tools:['inventory-tracker','unit-price','cash-flow'],sources:['storage'],sections:[
{title:'Define one row as one distinct stock item',paragraphs:['A stock list needs a stable identifier. Use a unique SKU for each item or variant you need to distinguish, such as NOTE-A for one notebook type. Two products with different sizes or costs should not share a row merely because their names are similar.','Record a physical count in a consistent unit: pieces, boxes or another clearly understood stock unit. The quantity field uses whole numbers, so define the row’s unit before entering the amount. The tool is a manual browser list, not a shared warehouse database or a system that automatically updates after a sale.']},
{title:'Understand the value calculation',paragraphs:['Recorded stock value is quantity multiplied by entered unit cost. If 12 notebooks cost NPR 80 each, the modeled value is 960. Four pens at 20 contribute 80, and three bags at 450 contribute 1350. The combined value is NPR 2390.','That value reflects your chosen cost basis. It is not automatically retail revenue, profit, tax valuation or a formal accounting inventory value. Use a consistent cost definition and one currency throughout. The tool rejects totals too large for its exact minor-unit arithmetic.']},
{title:'Treat a reorder flag as a prompt',paragraphs:['An item is flagged when recorded quantity is at or below its entered reorder threshold. If the threshold is five and quantity is four, the row asks for review. A quantity of five also triggers the threshold. This is a simple comparison, not a demand forecast or an automatic purchase order.','Set thresholds using your actual needs, lead times and stock process. The tool cannot know supplier reliability, seasonal demand, reserved stock or incoming orders. Verify the shelf and outstanding orders before purchasing.'],list:['Enter a unique SKU and descriptive item name.','Record the current whole-unit count.','Enter unit cost and a deliberate reorder threshold.','Review value totals and low-stock flags.','Export CSV and a JSON backup after a verified count.']},
{title:'Make updates traceable',paragraphs:['A browser list becomes stale when sales, damage or deliveries are not recorded. Choose a routine for recounting and updating it. Keep source receipts or another appropriate business record outside the tool; a revised quantity does not preserve a complete transaction history.','Optional local storage belongs to one site origin and browser profile. It can disappear when site data is cleared and cannot resolve simultaneous edits from several employees. Export a backup if the list matters. If the business needs audit history, access controls, barcode workflows or multiuser synchronization, move to a system designed for those requirements instead of stretching a manual utility beyond its purpose.']}
]},
{slug:'business-card-vcard-qr-print',title:'Make a business card with a contact QR people can verify',category:'business',summary:'Keep the visual card readable, distinguish a vCard from a website link and test both the printed and digital contact.',tools:['business-card','qr-code','contrast-checker'],sources:['qrBorder','printing'],sections:[
{title:'Prioritize the contact action',paragraphs:['A useful business card makes the name and preferred contact route easy to find. Start with the person or brand, role and the details people actually need. A long list of handles can compete with the main action. Use short labels and check spelling before adjusting colors.','The maker creates an 85 × 55 mm card layout. That is the tool’s editable output format, not a guarantee that every printer accepts it without bleed or trimming requirements. Ask the printing service for its specifications before ordering a batch.']},
{title:'Understand the QR payload',paragraphs:['The optional QR contains a vCard contact record, rather than a tracking redirect. It includes the entered name and available contact fields. A scanner may offer to create a contact, but downloading a VCF or generating the code does not modify an address book automatically.','More contact text makes a denser QR. Keep details concise and scan the preview. If the QR becomes difficult to use at card size, reduce unnecessary fields or choose a simpler web-address code in a separate workflow. Do not remove the quiet-zone border to make the code appear larger.']},
{title:'Check digital details before the print',paragraphs:['Enter the phone in a form a recipient can understand, including the country code when appropriate. Use the intended email and full website address. The sample details are demonstration data and should be replaced, not printed as if they were yours.'],list:['Enter concise name, role and company details.','Add only the contact fields you want to share.','Choose the accent color and optional vCard QR.','Generate and read the entire card at a realistic size.','Download the VCF and inspect its fields in a trusted contact application.','Scan a printed sample before ordering more copies.']},
{title:'Use the right master file',paragraphs:['PNG gives a rendered pixel copy, SVG retains vector elements and text, and PDF preserves the tool’s intended physical card dimensions. A font can be substituted when an SVG is opened elsewhere. Inspect the exact file your printer receives and verify its print scale and margins.','Keep the editable contact data so later changes do not require reconstructing it from a QR image. A printed card cannot update a contact record already saved on someone’s phone. Avoid putting private information into a public card, and check the destination website on a phone. The generator creates files locally; it does not validate professional credentials, deliver emails or guarantee compatibility with every scanning application.']}
]},
{slug:'shipping-address-label-no-postage',title:'Print a clear address label and keep postage separate',category:'business',summary:'Choose a physical label size, preserve every address line and verify the recipient before attaching it to a parcel.',tools:['shipping-label','business-card','qr-code'],sources:['printing','page'],sections:[
{title:'An address label is not a shipping purchase',paragraphs:['The label maker lays out sender and recipient addresses with a package reference and optional note. It does not buy postage, book a carrier, create tracking or prepare a customs declaration. Those steps belong to the carrier’s official process. A decorative QR or reference does not substitute for a carrier-issued barcode.','Check the destination country’s address conventions and the carrier’s required information. Use the full recipient details and a return address that is appropriate for the shipment. Do not use the sample recipient or demonstration reference on a real package.']},
{title:'Select the actual paper or label size',paragraphs:['The tool offers 100 × 150 mm, 4 × 6 inch, A4 and US Letter layouts. Four inches is 101.6 mm, so 4 × 6 inches is close to, but not exactly, 100 × 150 mm. Choose the size your printer and label stock actually use.','For A4 or Letter, the label sits on the larger sheet. Review the PDF at actual size and check that no content falls outside the printable area. A printer’s fit setting can alter the physical dimensions. Print a sample on ordinary paper before using adhesive stock.']},
{title:'Preserve the address, not just the layout',paragraphs:['Enter sender and recipient lines in the intended order. The layout wraps long lines and limits the number that fit. If the tool asks you to shorten an address, do not delete essential information merely to pass the limit; use a more appropriate label workflow or an accepted abbreviation.','The reference helps your own parcel identification. It is not a tracking number unless a carrier has issued it as one. Keep delivery notes concise and avoid including sensitive information that anyone handling the package could read.'],list:['Confirm the recipient name and complete address.','Enter the return address.','Choose the matching physical output size.','Generate and read every wrapped line.','Print at the intended scale and inspect the result.','Follow the carrier’s separate postage and customs process.']},
{title:'Check the package after attaching the label',paragraphs:['Place the label on a clear surface where it remains readable. Remove or cover obsolete address labels according to the carrier’s instructions, and keep required carrier markings visible. A correct new label can still be confusing if an old destination is left beside it.','The PDF, PNG and SVG downloads contain the addresses you entered, so store and share them appropriately. The tool does not send the parcel details to a delivery service. Keep any carrier receipt and tracking record separately. If the shipment has special handling, international documentation or regulated contents, use the carrier’s current requirements rather than relying on a generic address layout.']}
]},
{slug:'count-nepali-cash-notes-coins',title:'Count Nepali notes and coins with a denomination check',category:'nepal',summary:'Separate note and coin rows, verify the piece count and reconcile a worked NPR total.',tools:['npr-cash-counter','nepali-words','budget-planner'],sources:['nrbNotes','nrbCash'],sections:[
{title:'Sort before entering quantities',paragraphs:['A denomination counter is most useful after the physical cash has been sorted. Make separate piles for each note value and for coins. Enter quantities of pieces, rather than the money value of each pile. For example, three NPR 100 notes means quantity 3 in the 100-note row, not 300.','The common view includes regularly encountered notes and separate NPR 1 and NPR 2 coin rows. An optional view adds uncommon older note denominations. Nepal Rastra Bank’s denomination information includes older 1, 2, 25 and 250 notes that are no longer newly issued; that does not by itself label an existing note invalid. Verify questions about validity directly with NRB.']},
{title:'Use both amount and piece count',paragraphs:['Consider two 1000 notes, one 500 note, three 100 notes, two 20 notes, one 5 note, four 2 coins and two 1 coins. The amounts are 2000 + 500 + 300 + 40 + 5 + 8 + 2 = NPR 2855. The piece count is 2 + 1 + 3 + 2 + 1 + 4 + 2 = 15.','The piece count provides a second check. If the money total looks right but the number of physical pieces differs, revisit the denomination quantities. Keeping coins and notes in distinct rows avoids treating a coin pile as a note pile when recounting.'],table:{headers:['Pieces','Subtotal NPR'],rows:[['2 × 1000 notes','2000'],['1 × 500 note','500'],['3 × 100 notes','300'],['2 × 20 notes + 1 × 5 note','45'],['4 × 2 coins + 2 × 1 coins','10'],['Total: 15 pieces','2855']]}},
{title:'Recount a discrepancy methodically',paragraphs:['If your expected cash is NPR 3000 and the entered total is 2855, the arithmetic difference is 145. That does not establish whether money is missing: the expected amount, physical count or typed quantities could be wrong. Check one denomination at a time and compare the table with the piles.'],list:['Sort notes and coins into clear groups.','Enter a whole-number quantity for each denomination.','Enable uncommon note rows only when relevant.','Calculate and compare subtotals with the piles.','Export the CSV if a count record is useful.']},
{title:'Keep the counter’s scope clear',paragraphs:['The utility does not authenticate currency, inspect security features or reconcile a bank account. It also does not record a transaction history. Use the appropriate bank or business process for authenticity checks and formal cash reconciliation.','A downloaded count is a snapshot of your entries. Add the count date and responsible person in your own records if needed, without exposing unnecessary personal information. Recount important cash independently and keep the source records. For a written total, use the Nepali number-words tool and verify the wording against the numeric amount before adding it to a document.']}
]},
{slug:'nepali-bs-calendar-ad-dates-holidays',title:'Read a Nepali BS calendar with AD dates and scoped holiday notes',category:'nepal',summary:'Use the supported date range, check a known conversion and distinguish a dated holiday from a universal closure.',tools:['nepali-calendar','bs-ad-converter','nepali-holidays'],sources:['nepaliDates','moha'],sections:[
{title:'Treat BS month lengths as data',paragraphs:['The Bikram Sambat calendar is not converted accurately by adding a fixed number of years and months to an AD date. Month lengths vary, so this tool uses a bundled month-length table. Its supported range is BS 2000–2090. Requests outside that range need a different verified source rather than a guessed extrapolation.','Choose the BS year and month to generate a calendar. Each day also displays an AD month-day reference. The printable header states the AD start and end dates, which helps when a BS month crosses an AD month boundary. You can choose Nepali or English day numerals without changing the underlying dates.']},
{title:'Check a known date before using a schedule',paragraphs:['BS 2083-01-01 corresponds to AD 2026-04-14, a Tuesday. BS 2083-07-01 corresponds to 2026-10-18. Under the bundled conversion table, AD 2026-10-28 is BS 2083-07-11. These examples make it easier to notice a wrong selected year or a date-format mix-up.','Write the calendar system beside dates in important records. A string such as 2083-07-11 should be labeled BS, while 2026-10-28 should be labeled AD. Do not assume that a receiving form interprets a date the same way as the calendar you are viewing.']},
{title:'Read holiday scope before planning a closure',paragraphs:['The bundled holiday overlay is limited to dated records from the Ministry of Home Affairs notice for BS 2083. Some holidays apply to a region, community, institution or group. A named date in a list does not automatically mean every office, school or business closes.','The tool includes available scope notes on additional printable pages. Other supported years still have calendar dates, but no verified holiday overlay is claimed for them. Consult the official notice and relevant institution for changes or a decision that depends on a closure.'],list:['Choose a supported BS year and month.','Review the AD start date and first weekday.','Inspect holiday notes and their scope for 2083.','Download the calendar and any additional notes.','Use the CSV when you need an explicit BS–AD mapping for the month.']},
{title:'Keep the export’s limits visible',paragraphs:['A printed page is a snapshot of the bundled data. It will not change if an official notice is later amended. Record the source and check the current official notice before travel, an exam, a payment deadline or another important commitment.','The PDF uses rendered pages to preserve Nepali-script appearance. That is useful for visual consistency, but it does not create a fully structured, selectable-text calendar document. Keep the CSV for machine-readable date mapping. For a single date conversion, use the dedicated date tool and verify the calendar-system labels before copying the result into another application.']}
]},
{slug:'write-edit-nepali-request-letter',title:'Draft a Nepali request letter, then make it your own',category:'nepal',summary:'Choose an editable school, office or general request template and check dates, wording and the final PDF.',tools:['nepali-letter','nepali-calendar','text-formatter'],sources:['printing'],sections:[
{title:'Use a template as a starting point',paragraphs:['A useful request letter explains who is writing, what is requested and why the recipient can act on it. The generator provides original editable templates for school leave, office leave and a general request. They are not official government forms and do not guarantee acceptance by any institution.','If the recipient requires its own form or an online process, use that process. For an ordinary letter, gather the recipient’s correct title, institution, address, applicant details and relevant dates before drafting. Avoid including private medical or family details that are unnecessary for the request.']},
{title:'Make the date system unambiguous',paragraphs:['The default date uses the supported BS conversion when available and identifies it as बी.सं. Review it rather than assuming the default suits every submission. Enter leave start and end dates in a consistent calendar system and label them when the recipient might otherwise be unsure.','For a two-day leave request, check whether both endpoints are included under the institution’s rules. The template does not calculate an approved leave balance or determine eligibility. Keep the request aligned with the actual dates and the receiving organization’s policy.']},
{title:'Edit the generated text before exporting',paragraphs:['School and office templates assemble a respectful request around the reason and leave dates. General request mode lets you write the subject and requested action directly. After generation, the full letter remains editable so you can correct wording, grammar, tone and line breaks.','Read the letter from the recipient’s perspective. Is the requested action specific? Is the applicant identifiable? Is a contact route needed? Remove demonstration details such as नमुना विद्यालय and replace them with the real institution. A short clear letter is often easier to act on than a long generic paragraph.'],list:['Choose the letter type.','Replace the sample recipient and applicant details.','Enter the request, dates and any necessary explanation.','Generate the draft and proofread the editable final text.','Download TXT for future editing or prepare printable pages.']},
{title:'Review the printed appearance and submission route',paragraphs:['The printable export embeds a bundled Nepali font into the page design so Nepali-script shaping can be rendered consistently. The resulting PDF is image-based for that appearance; keep the TXT file when editable or selectable text is required. Inspect names, joined letters, dates and page breaks in the actual output.','Add a signature only when the recipient accepts that workflow, and follow any attachment requirements. Downloading the letter does not submit it or send an email. Keep a copy of the final version and use the institution’s stated submission channel. If the wording has legal, employment or other significant consequences, obtain appropriate help rather than assuming a generic template addresses those circumstances.']}
]}
];
